BE IT ORDAINED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING:
Section 1.
That the owners of the 2,349.54-acre property described in Exhibit A to this
Ordinance have submitted a Sweetgrass Planned Unit Development (“PUD”) amendment pursuant to
Sections 2.2.2, 2.4.1 and 5.6.2 of the Cheyenne Unified Development Code (“UDC”) which would
amend the Sweetgrass PUD regulating plan which was approved by the Governing Body on June 11,
2018 by Ordinance No. 4232.
Section 2.
That on August 5, 2019, the City of Cheyenne Planning Commission conducted a
public hearing, reviewed the Applicant’s proposed amendments to the Sweetgrass PUD that are the
subject of this Ordinance, found that it met the 15 review criteria for approval of the PUD amendments,
and recommended approval of said PUD amendments shown in Exhibit B to this Ordinance without
conditions.
Section 3.
That the Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne finds that the proposed
Sweetgrass PUD amendments that are the subject of this Ordinance meets the 15 review criteria
specified in Section 2.2.2.d of the UDC for a PUD text amendment.
Section 4.
That, in accordance with Section 2.2.2, Planned Development Plan, Section 2.4.1,
Zoning Text Amendment, and Section 5.6.2 PUD
— Planned Unit Development Text Amendment, of
the UDC, the amendments are hereby approved, and the “Sweetgrass Final Planned Unit Development
Standards and Guidelines, 1st Amendment” described in Exhibit B to this Ordinance is hereby approved.
Section 5.
That, in accordance with Section 5.6.2, the land use, design and development
standards and guidelines described in Exhibit B to this Ordinance shall govern this Sweetgrass PUD
zoning classification.
Section 6.
Sections, paragraphs, sentences, clauses and phrases ofthis Ordinance are severable.
If any section, paragraph, sentence, clause, or phrase of this Ordinance is declared unconstitutional, such
unconstitutionality shall not affect any of the remaining sections, paragraphs, sentences, clauses, and
phrases.
Section 8.
That this Ordinance shall be in full force and effect upon its approval and
publication.
