•
The northern Village Center provides 1.35-acres of private open space. Public greenways
Tracts D, E and F include another 2.17-acres of trails.
•
The southern residential neighborhood provides 3.37-acres of private open space and
2.62-acres of public greenway trails in Tracts H,], K and L.
This PUD 1 amendment would allow residential uses within the Village Center block of that 1
Filing subdivision in the form of live/work units and/or residences over shops (dwellings over
commercial spaces).
This amendment would also provide a new set of design standards for
buildings located within the Village Center and would allow increased building heights within the
Village Center, from 40-feet to 55-feet, and within the Events Center, from 60-feet to 80-feet.
These design standards reflect the design vision of the Lummis family for that community
commercial center. Lastly, the amendment incorporates minor boundary adjustments for the
Village Center and Events Center Parcels C, D, CC and Tract 6 (see Attachment D).
Separately, the Applicant has submitted a “2 Filing” subdivision for the Sweetgrass community.
This
2nd Filing application (UDC-19-00393) proposes to create a new 26.41-acre single-block
subdivision with three lots: Lots 1, 2 and 3. Lots 1 and 2 would accommodate small commercial
development and Lot 3 would accommodate a large commercial “event center” (hotel and
meeting rooms, with a large parking lot).
