### Page 9 of 160

```text
This 2nd Filing is the second phase of the Sweetgrass Community Preliminary P/at approved in
October 2017 (UDC-17-00543). The overall Sweetgrass Preliminary Plat proposed 10 phases of
development. The Sweetgrass 1 Filing Final Plat was the first phase and was approved by City
Council in June 2018 and was recorded with the County Clerk in January 2019.
This proposed PUD amendment has the followinglo9 elements:
1.
It would allow increased building heights for the hotel and events center from 60-feet to
80-feet (Section 4, Table 8);
2.
It defines how building heights are measured (Section 2.C.1);
3.
It defines the use called Micro-Brewery and allows it in the Village Center and Events
Center subareas (Sec. 2.C.13);
4.
It removes the City from enforcement of fence designs and standards, leaving it to the
Design Review Committee (DRC) to permit ad enforce.
If the DRC disbands, the UDC
fence regulations would apply which the City would enforce (Sec. 3.A.11 and 3.B.4);
5.
In the High-Density Residential (HDR) zone, detached garages and carports are allowed
and are not considered accessory structures (Sec. 4, Table 4);
6. The following land uses were added to the Village Center block: restaurants, live/work
and apartments over commercial uses (Sec. 4.2.a);
7.
The boundaries of the Village Center and Events Center subareas were adjusted to
accommodate development of a hotel and convention/meeting facility in the Events Center
subarea (Parcels C, D, CC and Tract 6 adjustments);
8.
Village Center design standards were added and placed in an Appendix D (Sec. 4.2.d);
9.
Appendix D was added to list the architectural standards and guidelines for the Village
Center to reflect a “Modern Farm House” concept for the block (see Attachment D for
image examples); and, lastly,
10. the proposed PUD amendment re-formats the document and changes the name to the
“Sweetgrass Final Planned Unit Development Standards and Guidelines 1 Amendment”
with a date of June 25, 2019.
These changes to the 2018-adopted PUD can be deemed minor within the scope and scale of the
overall Sweetgrass PUD and its proposed development. However, due to the scale of the overall
Sweetgrass PUD and community, we are evaluating these 1 amendments by the PUD Final Plan
15 review criteria of UDC Section 2.2.2.d (Planned Development
— Regulating Plan or
Development Master Plan), pursuant to UDC Section 5.6.2.g,
and this report contains
that evaluation.
Each of the 15 review criteria are important measurements as to how
development allowed by the proposed PUD amendments would be consistent with City
policies,
would
be
compatible
with
surrounding
developments,
what
quality
of
development would result within the PUD land area, and how the City would provide
essential
services to the
new development.
The proposed Sweetgrass
PUD 1
Amendment positively addresses those 15 review criteria as noted below.
Due to meeting the 15 review criteria of Section 2.22.d of the UDC, the Planning
Commission recommends approvalofthis PUD1 amendmentto the Governing Body.
