Complies.
The proposed amendments strengthen the land uses and design of the Village
Center to reflect the vision the Applicant has for this commercial hub for the Sweetgrass
community. The amendments reflect sound planning.
5.
The application meets the purposes, intent, and all applicable standards in
Article 4.
Complies.
The proposed PUD amendments incorporate by reference 43 standards of the UDC
Article 4 which are listed in Appendix C.
Another reference in the PUD states that if the PUD
regulations are “silent” on a
particular development or design standard of a proposed
development or permit application, the applicable UDC standard in effect at the time of the permit
application would be applicable to measure the proposed development. For example, the PUD is
“silent” on subdivision standards and processes; therefore, the UDC Article 2 provisions for
subdivisions in effect at the time of the application would apply. The proposed amendment also
removes the special fence standards from City enforcement, at the Department’s request. Rather,
the Sweetgrass Design Review Committee (DRC) would permit and enforce the PUD fence
standards.
If the DRC is ever disbanded, the PUD states that the City’s UDC fence regulations
would apply and the City would enforce those standards.
6.
Aflyphasingproposedin the application is dearlyindicatedand demonstrates
a logical and well-planned development pattern.
This may indude
consideration ofamenities andpublic facilities ofthe subdivision within each
phase compared to the anticipated timing or the likelihood of future phases
being constructed as planned.
Complies:
Sheet 5 of 6 of the PUD Maps (see Attachment C) includes a Phasing Plan which
does not change with this amendment. At this time, Sweetgrass is intended to be built out over
10 phases, with an assumed five years per phase. It is anticipated that the pace of development
and sequencing will change over time due to market forces and the timing of infrastructure
improvements beyond the Applicant’s control. Therefore, updated Phasing Plans may be provided
periodically for the purposes of coordination between the land owners, the City, and other
interested parties.
